--
-- NEW CONTENT (Debug Area, DA-10): the NPC lineup in the east wing of world
-- 1300's south compound (docs/content/debug-area.md#npc-lineup).
--
-- Id block: templates 1410-1599 (DA-10). One appearance-only clone of every
-- distinct character look in entity_templates, plus one default-dressed NPC
-- for each of the six character body sets no template uses. A look is the
-- body set, the component set (in any order), the two colours, the skin
-- tint and the static mesh (NULL and '' are the same); props
-- (GLB_Components.*) and deployables and mines (WP-Human.*) are not
-- characters. The source is the lowest template id with that look, named in
-- the comment above each row.
--
-- A clone copies the source's body set, components, colours, skin tint,
-- static mesh, level and name_id (so the nameplate reads like the source's;
-- a source with no name_id has a blank nameplate, and its template_name is
-- kept in `name`). Everything else is fixed: faction 1 (World Object,
-- friendly: players cannot attack it, and no faction in the reaction table
-- is hostile to it, so it never starts or joins an NPC-vs-NPC fight), class
-- mob, event set 570 (the default sequence set 150 of the 155 sources and
-- the DA-09 lords carry), and no ability set, loot, vendor lists, dialog,
-- interaction sets, patrol or wander.
--
-- The six template-less body sets are dressed from resources.body_components
-- (every component listed for the set, or the base head, torso, legs, hands
-- and boots for HM_Mesh.HM_BodySet, whose parts carry no slot names).
--
-- Rows are in walk order: humans, Jaffa, Goa'uld, Asgard, children,
-- creatures, machines; inside a group by body set, then by source template
-- id. A template added later with a new look fails
-- live_db_debug_area_lineup until it gets a row here and a spawn in
-- spawnlist_debug_area_lineup.sql.
--
-- Humans, male
-- source 10 Col Marsh (pet)
